BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:surf-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sanford Underground Research Facility: Artist-in-Residenc
 e Program 2027 (Lead\, South Dakota)
DESCRIPTION:The SURF Artist-in-Residence program invites artists to create 
 work inspired by the Sanford Underground Research Facility in Lead\, South
  Dakota. At 4\,850 feet deep\, SURF is the deepest underground laboratory 
 in the United States\, housed in the former Homestake Gold Mine\, and host
 s experiments in physics\, biology\, geology and engineering.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Sanford Underground Research Facility (SURF)\nLocation: Sanford Under
 ground Research Facility\, Lead\, South Dakota\, USA\, in the Black Hills.
  The call does not state a residency or nationality restriction\; travel\,
  housing and per diem for both visits are covered.\nAward: USD 5\,000 stip
 end paid in two installments\, plus up to USD 5\,000 in additional funds t
 he artist may apply for to create the artwork. Transportation (airfare\, r
 ental car or mileage)\, housing and per diem are covered for both visits\;
  a studio space and guided surface and underground tours are provided\; re
 turn shipping of the exhibition is covered up to USD 7\,000.\nDuration: Fo
 ur-week on-site residency in summer 2027 (scheduled between 22 May and 31 
 July in coordination with SURF)\, plus a one-week exhibition installation 
 and guest-lecture visit in October 2027.\n\nMore: https://sanfordlab.org/p
 rograms/SURFAiR?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sanfordlab.org/programs/SURFAiR?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sanford Underground Research Facility\, Lead\, South Dakota\, USA\
 , in the Black Hills. The call does not state a residency or nationality r
 estriction\; travel\, housing and per diem for both visits are covered.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:simons-foundation-open-interval-turbulence-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Interval: An Artist-Scientist Exploration of Turbule
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Open Interval is a Simons Foundation program that supports trio
 s consisting of an artist\, a scientist\, and a representative from a 501(
 c)(3) arts organization to collaborate around a shared scientific theme. T
 he current cycle centers on the theme of turbulence\, a phenomenon at the 
 edge of chaos and beauty.\n\nOrganisation: Simons Foundation\nLocation: Un
 ited States (trio must be regionally co-located)\nAward: USD 30\,000 per a
 warded trio\nDuration: April to December 2027 (several months of collabora
 tion)\n\nMore: https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-ope
 n-interval-an-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-a
 n-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (trio must be regionally co-located)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mats-residency-program-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: MATS Residency Program: 6-24 Month Funded AI Safety Resea
 rch (Winter 2027 intake)
DESCRIPTION:The MATS Residency\, announced in August 2026 as a new track al
 ongside the seasonal MATS fellowship\, funds 6 to 24 months of high-indepe
 ndence AI safety research for experienced researchers\, whether already in
  AI safety or moving in from adjacent fields.\n\nOrganisation: MATS (ML Al
 ignment and Theory Scholars)\nLocation: In-person at MATS offices in Berke
 ley\, London\, or Washington DC\; visa support provided where required. Fo
 r experienced researchers with at least one substantial piece of research-
 caliber work.\nAward: USD 155\,000 to 285\,000 per year gross (set by loca
 tion\, seniority\, and experience)\, plus medical/dental/vision/life insur
 ance\, retirement plan\, paid time off\, conference funding\, catered meal
 s\, and up to USD 25\,000 relocation support. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: 6 to 24 months with rolling start dates\; three intake windows per year
 .\n\nMore: https://www.matsprogram.org/residency?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.matsprogram.org/residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:In-person at MATS offices in Berkeley\, London\, or Washington DC\
 ; visa support provided where required. For experienced researchers with a
 t least one substantial piece of research-caliber work.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wave-farm-research-production-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART:20261202T042900Z
DTEND:20261202T045900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 EST: Wave Farm: 2027 Research and Production Program
  (Transmission Art Residencies and Radio Art Fellowships\, NY)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nWave Farm\, the Warhol Foun
 dation-backed transmission arts center in Acra\, NY\, opens one applicatio
 n covering all its 2027 opportunities: the Transmission Art Residency\, th
 e Spatial Sound Residency\, and two Radio Art Fellowship tracks (Research\
 , and Community Engagement) connected to Wave Farm's WGXC radio station.\n
 \nOrganisation: Wave Farm\nLocation: Wave Farm\, Acra\, NY\, US (Catskill 
 Mountain Park). International open call.\nAward: USD 1\,000 stipend for ea
 ch 10-day residency\; USD 2\,000 for each two-month Radio Art Fellowship. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: 10 days (Transmission Art and Spatial Sound
  residencies) or 2 months (Radio Art Fellowships)\, during 2027.\n\nMore: 
 https://wavefarm.org/ta/residency-program/info-apply?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://wavefarm.org/ta/residency-program/info-apply?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wave Farm\, Acra\, NY\, US (Catskill Mountain Park). International
  open call.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eyebeam-agency-nyc-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Eyebeam AGENCY NYC Residency\, Spring 2027
DESCRIPTION:The NYC track of Eyebeam's AGENCY residency cycle supports New 
 York City-based artists exploring questions of agency at a moment when AI 
 systems increasingly act\, decide and carry out tasks on our behalf: how t
 o preserve human agency as these systems shape human behavior\, how to ass
 ert agency in imagining and building the societies we inhabit\, and what a
 gency becomes when understood as...\n\nOrganisation: Eyebeam\nLocation: Ne
 w York City\, USA. Applicants must live within the five boroughs and be ab
 le to work on site at Eyebeam at least one day a week for the full residen
 cy term (15 March to 11 June 2027).\nAward: USD 5\,000 stipend per selecte
 d artist\, plus mentorship and access to tools and technical expertise thr
 ough Eyebeam's network. No application fee (via Submittable).\nDuration: 1
 5 March to 11 June 2027\; on site at Eyebeam at least one day per week.\n\
 nMore: https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-nyc-residency?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-nyc-residency?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA. Applicants must live within the five boroughs
  and be able to work on site at Eyebeam at least one day a week for the fu
 ll residency term (15 March to 11 June 2027).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rome-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Rome: Rome Prize Fellowship 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:The Rome Prize supports roughly 30 artists and scholars a year 
 with a residential fellowship at the American Academy in Rome\; discipline
 s include Design and Visual Arts\, where media and new-genre work is regul
 arly funded. Fellows receive a USD 16\,000 (half-term) or USD 30\,000 (ful
 l-term) stipend plus housing\, workspace and weekday meals on the Academy'
 s Janiculum campus.\n\nOrganisation: American Academy in Rome\nLocation: R
 ome\, Italy (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisation with 
 NYC office). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreign nationa
 ls resident in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may apply onl
 y in certain categories.\nAward: Stipends of USD 16\,000 (half-term\, abou
 t 5 months) and USD 30\,000 (full-term\, about 10 months)\, plus housing\,
  workspace and weekday meals. Approximately 30 fellowships per year. APPLI
 CATION FEE: USD 50 by 1 November (USD 60 for multiple categories)\; USD 80
 /90 in the late window to 15 November.\nDuration: 5 or 10 months\n\nMore: 
 https://www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rome\, Italy (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisat
 ion with NYC office). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreig
 n nationals resident in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may 
 apply only in certain categories.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:generator-residency-winter-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Generator Residency (Kairos x Constellation\, Winter 2027
 )
DESCRIPTION:A three-month residency for AI safety generalists: builders\, o
 perators and organizers rather than researchers. Residents pitch\, build a
 nd ship their own projects with weekly advice from field leaders\, then ge
 t support landing a full-time AI safety role.\n\nOrganisation: Kairos and 
 Constellation\nLocation: Berkeley\, California\, USA (Constellation office
 ). Core residency is in person\; J-1 visa sponsorship available for most i
 nternational applicants.\nAward: USD 8\,500 per month stipend (some Embedd
 ed track residents employed at a roughly equivalent salary)\, plus travel 
 to and from Berkeley. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 months full-time (1
 8 January to 9 April 2027)\; selected residents can extend in person until
  late May and remotely until early July 2027.\n\nMore: https://generatorre
 sidency.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://generatorresidency.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berkeley\, California\, USA (Constellation office). Core residency
  is in person\; J-1 visa sponsorship available for most international appl
 icants.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
